 "asked_at": "2026-10-18T00:45+08:00",
 "answer": "Yes, the haze situation in Singapore is currently **bad**. \n\nAir quality has remained in the **\"Unhealthy\" to \"Very Unhealthy\"** range across the island due to transboundary smoke haze drifting from fires in Sumatra and Kalimantan, Indonesia. \n\nKey details on the air quality conditions:\n* **PSI Levels:** The 24-hour Pollutant Standards Index (PSI) has remained elevated, pushing into the \"Very Unhealthy\" band in parts of the island (such as the West) and staying firmly in the \"Unhealthy\" band across other regions. \n* **PM2.5 Concentrations:** 1-hour PM2.5 readings have frequently spiked into the \"High\" and \"Elevated\" bands. \n\n**Health Advisories:**\n* **Healthy persons** are advised to reduce or avoid strenuous outdoor physical activities.\n* **Elderly, pregnant women, children, and those with chronic heart or lung conditions** should minimize or completely avoid outdoor activities, and consider wearing a mask if heading outdoors is unavoidable. \n\nYou can check real-time updates, local PSI numbers, and hourly PM2.5 readings directly via the **myENV app** or the official National Environment Agency (NEA) haze microsite at [www.haze.gov.sg](https://www.haze.gov.sg).",
